MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_001: Whoa...
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_002: What is it, Mu? You've been staring at me for\nrather a long time.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_003: Oh, sorry! I didn't mean to do that. Rude of me.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_004: I was just looking at your clothes and accessories\nand stuff. They're beautiful!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_005: You think so? These are all garments and\nadornments I brought from my home county.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_006: Well, they're gorgeous! And they really suit you!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_007: You honor me with your praise! Why, yes, my\naesthetic sensibilities are quite impressive.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_008: Perhaps you'd like one of my jewels? I'd be more\nthan happy to give you one!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_009: What?! You sure you want to give it up that easily?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_010: Oh, it's nothing special, really—just a bauble from\nthe family home.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_011: But you're from a prestigious house. Everything in\nyour home must have been real fancy!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_012: I can't take something that expensive for free.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_013: But I already told you you could have it! Hmm.\nVery well, I won't force it on you.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_014: How about this? Starting today, would you become\nmy steward?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_015: Your steward? Like, someone who looks after you?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_016: Among other things! You would carry my belongings,\nassist with errands I have, perhaps brew my tea...
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_017: Someone of your calm, attentive demeanor would be\nideal for the role!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_018: And as recompense for your work, I would give you\nthe jewel. Would you object to that arrangement?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_019: Aha! It seems even more brilliant when I say\nit aloud. What say you?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_020: OK. I don't mind doing that kinda stuff, so it's\nworth a shot.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_021: But I still think that jewel is too good of a reward for\nthis job.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_022: I'll feel better about it if you have me do things\nthat are, y'know...jewel worthy.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_023: You modest thing, you! I am charmed more and more\nby your attitude.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_C_024: Very well—consider yourself hired. See you soon,\nmy new steward!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_001: Olympia, I'll carry your shopping bags.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_002: Thank you, my wonderfully conscientious\nsteward!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_003: No problem! Am I doing this job well enough?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_004: Yes! I appreciate all your hard work, Mu.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_005: That lady's got jewelry on her jewelry! She's gotta\nbe loaded. This should be easy...
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_006: Ah! Get down!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_007: Mu?!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_008: Gah, flubbed it! Can't make a scene—time to get\noutta here.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_009: Olympia! Are you...OK?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_010: Yes, I'm alright, but forget about me! You're bleeding.\nWe must get that wound seen to, posthaste!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_011: I'm relieved the injury is so minor. But Mu, why did\nyou jump in to protect me?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_012: I don't know. My body just kinda...did it.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_013: Besides, I'm your steward, Olympia! It's only\nnatural I should protect you.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_014: Is that why? But that was all pretend!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_015: Not to me.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_016: I've been working for you, and I'm getting paid fairly\nfor that work.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_017: You're the perfect boss.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_018: But...it's not much of a reward.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_019: It's important to me that I always finish the\ncontract—like my mom and her mercenary work.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_020: You're so disciplined. And so stubborn! You're a\nstrong-willed woman, Mu.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_021: How could I treat someone so... Ahh...
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_022: Olympia? What's wrong?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_023: I've decided it's time that we put an end to our game\nof pretend.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_024: You needn't serve as my steward anymore.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_025: Oh! But—why? Did I screw something up?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_026: No, certainly not. I am truly grateful to you for saving\nmy life.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_027: And for that act, you deserve a generous reward.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_028: I think the jewel you refused the other day ought\nto suffice.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_029: Henceforth, let us treat one another as equals.\nNow, please rest up.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_B_030: But... It's over?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_001: Once again, I am struck by the realization that\nI barely recognize you now, Mu.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_002: That jewel I gave you those years ago—it would suit\nyou so well! Why do you not wear it?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_003: It's just too precious. I don't want to put it on before\npeace arrives.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_004: Stubborn as ever! All this time later, you're the\nsame old Mu.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_005: Hehe. I miss those days. It was fun being your\nsteward.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_006: Listen, Mu. While we're on the subject, I would like\nto ask you a favor.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_007: If I paid you with this, would you consider becoming\nmy steward again?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_008: Huh? Whoa, whoa! That's so much gold!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_009: It was easy enough to amass, with my talent for\nsinging and dancing...though I'll grant it took time.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_010: You earned all this on your own?! Sounds like\nhard work.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_011: Yes, to some extent it was. But I did not suffer in the\nearning of it.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_012: You see, the jewel I gave you was something I had\ntaken when I left home. It took no hardship or effort.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_013: Yet in spite of that, you showed me the same loyalty\nas you would an actual employer!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_014: So this time, I thought I'd reward you with something\nacquired through my own effort.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_015: It is a simple courtesy to extend to such a\ndiligent friend.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_016: I'm not sure I'm that special... I know I said I cared\nabout finishing the contract...
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_017: But really, I was just parroting what my mom said—\nborrowing her words.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_018: Mom started fighting in her teens and became a\nlegendary mercenary. I can't live up to that.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_019: If you're OK with me as I am, though...then I'll be\nyour steward again.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_020: Truly?!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_021: Of course! I shall brew you a pot of tea with\nlove, milady.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_022: How joyous! I know you will serve me ably.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_023: Heh. And I'm grown up now, so I know how to\ndo more stuff!
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_024: But I don't wanna be just any boring old steward...\nHow about I dress like a man again to attend you?
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_025: Oh, wonderful! Such a unique idea is suited to the\nBlue Rose of Caelus.
MID_SE_Moo_Oly_A_026: Here's to many more years of your faithful\nstewardship.